# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
paperbook/paperbook.db

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots, console logs, downloads).
# The knowledge-graph memory file at .claude/memory.jsonl is deliberately NOT
# ignored — it is committed so memory survives between web sessions.
.playwright-mcp/

# Live bot state — belongs on the `bot-state` branch, never on main.
# The favorite workflow restores these at the start of a run and pushes them
# back to bot-state at the end.
#
# These rules once listed executed_trades.csv / trade_history.csv /
# paper_trades*.csv, all of which were tracked anyway and force-added by the
# workflows (`git add -f`), so the file documented a policy nothing followed.
# What is listed here now is exactly what a running bot rewrites — tracking any
# of it on main as well is what broke the state-persist step (a dirty tree
# blocks the branch switch, after orders are already placed).
clv_sports.csv
CLV_SCOREBOARD.md
paper_trades_favorite.csv
paper_trades_sports.csv
sports_line_history.json
odds_quota.json
arb_scan.csv
executed_trades.csv
